1
00:00:12,480 --> 00:00:19,172
Mieux vaut acheter moins mais de meilleure qualité, plutôt que de renouveler sans cesse ses vêtements.
It's better to buy less but with better quality, rather than constantly renewing your clothes.

2
00:00:19,272 --> 00:00:25,028
Je m'oriente de plus en plus vers la seconde main au lieu de tout acheter neuf.
I'm turning more and more to second-hand instead of buying everything new.

3
00:00:25,128 --> 00:00:33,476
Pour les légumes, je privilégie les circuits courts. Il vaut mieux que les producteurs vendent directement.
For vegetables, I favour short supply chains. It's better that producers sell directly.

4
00:00:33,576 --> 00:00:40,100
Les labels aident, mais ils ne garantissent pas tout. Il faut rester vigilant.
Labels help, but they don't guarantee everything. You have to stay vigilant.

5
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:45,332
Réparer plutôt que jeter, c'est un réflexe qui s'apprend.
Repairing rather than throwing away is a reflex that can be learned.

6
00:00:45,432 --> 00:00:51,236
À force de faire attention, on finit par consommer autrement sans y penser.
By dint of paying attention, you end up consuming differently without thinking about it.
